 352:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 353:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 354:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT ring buffer
 355:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    and updates the associated write pointer which is periodically
 356:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    read by the host.
 357:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    The caller is responsible for managing the write chunk sizes as
 358:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    _WriteBlocking() will block until all data has been posted successfully.
 359:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 360:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 361:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pRing        Ring buffer to post to.
 362:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 363:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 364:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 365:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 366:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    >= 0 - Number of bytes written into buffer.
 367:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
