 416:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 417:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT ring buffer
 418:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    and updates the associated write pointer which is periodically
 419:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    read by the host.
 420:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    It is callers responsibility to make sure data actually fits in buffer.
 421:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 422:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 423:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pRing        Ring buffer to post to.
 424:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 425:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 426:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 427:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 428:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there might not be enough space in the "Up"-buffer, call _WriteBlocking
 429:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
