 734:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 735:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 736:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Reads characters from SEGGER real-time-terminal control block
 737:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    which have been previously stored by the application.
 738:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Used to do the same operation that J-Link does, to transfer
 739:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    RTT data via other channels, such as TCP/IP or UART.
 740:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 741:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 742:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of Up-buffer to be used.
 743:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to buffer provided by target application, to copy characters from RTT-up-
 744:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferSize   Size of the target application buffer.
 745:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 746:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 747:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes that have been read.
 748:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 749:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Additional information
 750:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function must not be called when J-Link might also do RTT.
 751:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function locks against all other RTT operations. I.e. during
 752:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    the read operation, writing is also locked.
 753:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    If only one consumer reads from the up buffer,
 754:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    call sEGGER_RTT_ReadUpBufferNoLock() instead.
 755:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
