 804:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** /*********************************************************************
 805:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 806:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock
 807:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 808:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 809:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 810:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block.
 811:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock does not lock the application
 812:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    and overwrites data if the data does not fit into the buffer.
 813:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 814:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 815:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 816:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 817:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 818:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 819:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 820:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, data is overwritten.
 821:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 822:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 823:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 824:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (3) Do not use SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock if a J-Link
 825:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        connection reads RTT data.
 826:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
 827:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** void SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock(unsigned BufferIndex, const void* pBuffer, unsigned NumByt
