 994:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 995:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 996:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 997:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block inside a <Down> buffer.
 998:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteDownBufferNoLock does not lock the application.
 999:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Used to do the same operation that J-Link does, to transfer
1000:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    RTT data from other channels, such as TCP/IP or UART.
1001:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1002:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1003:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Down"-buffer to be used.
1004:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
1005:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
1006:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1007:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1008:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Down"-buffer.
1009:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1010:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
1011:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) Data is stored according to buffer flags.
1012:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1013:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1014:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1015:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1016:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Additional information
1017:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function must not be called when J-Link might also do RTT.
1018:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
