1240:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
1241:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a single character/byte in SEGGER RTT buffer.
1242:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_PutCharSkipNoLock does not lock the application and
1243:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    skips the byte, if it does not fit into the buffer.
1244:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1245:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1246:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
1247:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    c            Byte to be stored.
1248:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1249:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1250:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
1251:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1252:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
1253:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, the character is dropped.
1254:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1255:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1256:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1257:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
